---
const prerender = true;

import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Head from "../../components/Head.astro";
import Logo from "../../images/Saturn.svg"

import PaymentForm from "../../components/PaymentForm.astro";

import "../../styles/project.css"
---

<BaseLayout renderHome={true}>
    <Head slot="head"
        title="Krystal - Saturn"
        description="Saturn is an upcoming open-source SAT solver with educational material attached.
            See our progress in making Saturn here."
        keywords="saturn, SATurn, sat solver, krystal saturn, krystal SATurn"
    />

    <main>
        <section>
            <h1>Saturn</h1>
            <img id="logo" src={Logo.src} alt="Saturn's logo"/>

            <div id="status-bar">
                <p>Status: Pre-release</p>
                <p id="middle">Version: N/A</p>
                <p>License: Unlicensed</p>
            </div>
            
            <p>
                Saturn is a complete SAT solver built in C++20. It is currently 
                educational material meant to teach others how SAT solvers operate
                and how they are implemented at a low level. While it is good enough 
                to be used as a standalone solver, it is most likely not competition 
                worthy, and we suggest other solvers to be used while we develop it
                further.
            </p>

            <p>
                As of now, Saturn isn't ready for release, and is unlicensed.
                Since it is  unlicensed, creating derivatives, distributing, and reproducing 
                any and all files is prohibited. However, since it's an educational project,
                this doesn't mean we disallow downloading/viewing/using any of the files. 
                You are 100% allowed to download, view, and use any and all of the files, but only 
                for personal use. If you are to download anything from the GitHub, you can do 
                anything you want <strong>but it must stay on your machine at all times.</strong>
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h1>Credits</h1>
            <p><strong>Developer:</strong> Oliver Lie</p>
            <p><strong>Educational Material Writer:</strong> Oliver Lie</p>
            <p>GitHub: 
                <a href="https://github.com/olie-ver/SATurn">
                    https://github.com/olie-ver/SATurn
                </a>
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h1>Support the Development</h1>
            <p>Here are some ways you can support the development of Saturn:</p>

            <h2>1. Ask Questions</h2>
            <p>
                Read through the educational materials and ask questions. Questions 
                like "why is X implemented this way," or "what happens if we change 
                X," would greatly help as we aim to answer them in our educational 
                materials. Reviewing the educational materials and suggesting 
                changes/revisions would be greatly appreciated.
            </p>

            <h2>2. Propose new Features</h2>
            <p>
                The world of SAT solving is very big and what is covered (DPLL and CDCL)
                is just scratching the surface. If you have an algorithm or heuristic
                you'd like to see implemented, let us know and we will do our best to 
                research, implement, and report our findings. 
            </p>

            <h2>3. Financial Support</h2>
            <p>
                Making a SAT solver isn't easy and it takes a lot of work, neither is 
                writing education materials on building your own. By donating to the
                development of Saturn, we can invest more time in its implementation 
                as well as its accompanying research report to make this knowledge more 
                accessible.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h1>Downloadable Files</h1>

            <ul>
                <li>
                    <a href=
                    "https://github.com/olie-ver/SATurn/raw/refs/heads/main/paper/From Scratch (First Draft).pdf">
                        From Scratch (First Draft)
                    </a>
                </li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
            <input id="show-form" type="checkbox"/>
            <label for="show-form">Click to Support</label>
            <span>
                <PaymentForm reason="Saturn"/>
            </span>
        </section>
    </main>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;

    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
    border-radius: 25px;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 8px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2), 0 6px 20px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.19);

    margin: 4% 0 0 10%;
    padding-bottom: 2.5%;
    width: 80%;
    height: fit-content;
    background: transparent;
    margin-bottom: 2svh;
    line-height: 1.7;
}

#logo {
   filter: var(--logo-filter);
}

#status-bar {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto auto auto;

    width: 90%;
    margin: 5% 5% 5% 5%;
    border-top: 3px solid var(--card-border-color);
    border-bottom: 3px solid var(--card-border-color);
}

#middle {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--card-border-color);
    border-right: 3px solid var(--card-border-color);
}

p {
    max-width: 80%;
}

code {
    text-align: left;
    width: 75%;
    color: #9ECBFF;
    background-color: #24292e;
}

span {
    color: #B392F0;
}

label~span {
    width: 100%;
}

#show-form, label~span {
    display: none;
}

#show-from, #show-form~label {
    align-self: center;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-bottom: 3svh;
}

#show-form~label {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: var(--text-color);
}

#show-form:checked~span {
    display: block;
}

ul {
    width: 75%;
}

li {
    text-align: left;
}

@media (orientation: landscape) {
    main {
        margin-left: calc(env(safe-area-inset-left));
    }
}
</style>
